DESIGN QUALITY ONLY. The anchor is chosen on four design criteria and explicitly NOT on the size of the resulting in-vitro discrepancy:
  (1) within-patient crossover, each subject their own control;
  (2) a DRUG-FREE baseline measured in the same patients, not a
      between-cohort contrast;
  (3) prospective rather than retrospective/observational;
  (4) earliest post-transplant (8-week treatment periods), therefore the
      least sympathetically reinnervated and the purest open-loop
      measurement. This is the same criterion the project already used
      when preferring the 36-month cohort over the 10-year one; applied
      consistently it selects Doesch over both.
